course: dictionary
lesson: 15118
title: Saltiness
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Saltiness is how salty something is. You can taste it on your tongue, and you can measure it in water. When you say «The saltiness of the soup was just right», you mean the soup had the right amount of salt.
explain: Saltiness also describes water. «The saltiness of the sea makes it easy to float» means there is so much salt in the water that your body rises up. The word does not mean the salt itself: it means how much salt there is.
explain: Look for clues around the word. If a sentence says «too much salt», «salty chips» or «taste», the word is probably about how salty something is. Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Saltiness is a noun, so it names a quality, like sweetness or softness.
fact: Saltiness is one of the basic tastes, along with sweet, sour, bitter and umami.
fact: The sea has different saltiness in different places, and the Dead Sea is so salty that people float easily in it.
fact: Too much saltiness is bad for your heart, which is why food labels show how much salt is in food.
fact: Scientists also call the saltiness of water its salinity.
exercise: «The chef tasted the soup and said the saltiness was just right.» What does saltiness mean here? | How loud a sound is | *How salty something tastes | How sweet something smells | How hot a drink is
exercise: Ella floated easily in the Dead Sea because of its saltiness. What does saltiness mean here? | How clean the sand is | How deep the water goes | *How much salt is in the water | How cold the water is
exercise: Which word is a basic taste, like saltiness? | *Sweetness | Loudness | Softness | Redness
test: «The crisps had so much saltiness that Sam drank a whole bottle of water.» What does saltiness mean? | How crispy the packet looks | How long the crisps last | *How salty something tastes | How crunchy something is
test: Which word means how much salt is in the sea? | Warmth | Sourness | *Saltiness | Brightness
exam: The food label shows the saltiness of the soup, so Mum checks it before she serves it. What does saltiness mean here? | Whether the soup is cold | *How much salt the soup has | How many bowls there are | How long the soup takes to cook
